{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786914879212},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to find out how many farmers markets the U.S. has per 100,000 residents using two data sources:\n1. US farmers markets by state 2026: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n2. Census file with population data: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\nThe task is to:\n1. Get total farmers markets from the first dataset\n2. Get total US population from the census file\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Present as one confident sentence with 4 decimal places\n5. Use tools to do math and verify everything\n\nFollowing the AGENTS.md instructions, I should:\n1. Orient first - check for semantic models with `xorq_semantic_models`\n2. Check existing aliases with `xorq_catalog_list_aliases`\n3. If no existing aliases cover this, I need to ingest the datasets\n4. Use `xorq_select` to get values\n5. Declare obligations and call `xorq_verify`\n\nLet me start by orienting - checking if there's a catalog and what's in it.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by orienting with the catalog and then ingesting the datasets."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HnQ4j4KqxZvunPFFN9Hfny","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path